WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.685
One platform, its organizations, and their customers. Each has data, context, and an

00:00:05.685 --> 00:00:11.100
agent. Guided proposals are labeled; validation and database execution are real.

00:00:13.101 --> 00:00:18.081
The platform exposes shipments and hides internal cost. The visual editor and agent

00:00:18.081 --> 00:00:21.081
both author the same serializable JSON definition.

00:00:23.081 --> 00:00:28.221
Active Pro organizations receive the lens. Delegation binds each organization on the

00:00:28.221 --> 00:00:30.791
server. The permission policy is JSON too.

00:00:32.794 --> 00:00:37.544
Andes narrows to Express shipments for active Gold customers who can read. Standard

00:00:37.544 --> 00:00:41.263
shipments disappear. The customer binding is added by the server.

00:00:43.805 --> 00:00:49.270
Sofía can use both providers. Mateo cannot use this Gold-only lens. Switching context

00:00:49.270 --> 00:00:52.035
changes the catalog and the available data.

00:00:54.036 --> 00:00:58.789
Which shipments need intervention? Start with nested shipment conditions. The authored

00:00:58.789 --> 00:01:03.266
predicate is validated and combined with inherited restrictions before execution.

00:01:05.266 --> 00:01:10.480
These shipments have deliberately different histories. One long hold, repeated shorter

00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:15.573
holds, tied delays, and empty histories. Counts and totals select different records.

00:01:15.573 --> 00:01:17.756
Inspect the real grouped query plan.

00:01:20.661 --> 00:01:25.768
Filter customs holds, sort by delay, skip the worst, and inspect the next. This

00:01:25.768 --> 00:01:29.131
general window runs through check on scoped records.

00:01:31.132 --> 00:01:36.278
Now read the notes. Customs has released one shipment, but broker and carrier disagree

00:01:36.278 --> 00:01:41.365
about who books pickup. Another awaits a scheduled laboratory review. Similar delays;

00:01:41.365 --> 00:01:42.502
different problems.

00:01:44.502 --> 00:01:49.608
The guided inference tags an ownership handoff and cites its evidence. Live inference

00:01:49.608 --> 00:01:54.775
uses the prompt when a model key is configured. These are in-memory entity, attribute,

00:01:54.775 --> 00:01:59.702
value records, with an explanation and expiry. Nothing is written to the database.

00:02:01.702 --> 00:02:07.094
The lens connects two field maps through a one-to-many bridge. One predicate combines

00:02:07.094 --> 00:02:12.359
Express priority, repeated holds, and an inferred handoff. Add a ranked window: two

00:02:12.359 --> 00:02:17.687
matches become one. Expire the facts, and that match disappears. Evaluation stays in

00:02:17.687 --> 00:02:18.132
memory.

00:02:20.132 --> 00:02:25.404
Try hiding internal cost inside an OR branch. The actual validator rejects it. Ask for

00:02:25.404 --> 00:02:30.063
another customer: the bound identity stays fixed and the query returns zero.

00:02:32.062 --> 00:02:37.245
Change Pacific to Starter. Its lens disappears and the earlier answer becomes stale.

00:02:37.245 --> 00:02:39.282
Run again: only Andes can answer.

00:02:41.283 --> 00:02:46.578
Lenses, permissions, predicates, and derived facts are JSON. Inspect them, change

00:02:46.578 --> 00:02:49.913
them, and watch the runtime enforce the boundaries.
